{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"arbored-demurrable-whippet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nIn a controlled plan-review study, rebar emitted **multiple separate findings that independent\nclassifiers judged to be one and the same issue**. Across 10 plan reviews (one rebar run each,\n`bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`, runner `pydantic_ai`), rebar emitted **139 findings that\nreduce to 122 distinct issues — +13.9% inflation**. It is not evenly spread:\n\n| run (study id) | emitted | distinct | inflation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ts-carbon-dsx-card-web-component` | 15 | 10 | **+50%** |\n| `ts-strata-paidleave-rfi-staff-experience` | 15 | 11 | **+36%** |\n| `ruby-mn-deed-casemgmt-outbound-writeback` | 9 | 7 | **+29%** |\n| `jira-dso-legacy-code-remediation` | 18 | 15 | **+20%** |\n| `java-opensearch-adaptive-concurrency` | 19 | 18 | +6% |\n| `jira-dso-strata-sdk-planning-context` | 19 | 18 | +6% |\n| `scss-uswds-elements-dsx-token-migration` | 20 | 19 | +5% |\n| `java-gradle`, `java-iceberg`, `ts-strata-sdk-cm-signal-coverage` | — | — | 0% |\n\n\"Same issue\" is not my judgment: each run was classified by **three independent judges** who\nanswered a generated list of relation candidates, and a pair was merged only on a **2-of-3\nmajority**. 16 duplicate groups resulted.\n\n## Which findings duplicated, and from which criteria\n\nThe recurring shape is **a specific criterion and a generic one reporting the same defect**. In\n**13 of 16** groups at least one member came from `G1G2` (edit-set/scope accuracy) or `G6`\n(approach soundness). Full inventory (`id` is the per-finding id in the verdict JSON):\n\n**`ts-strata-paidleave-rfi-staff-experience`** (4 groups)\n- fulfill-endpoint idempotency: `f02d0cd5760121153` [T5b,T9] + `f50f3f76a15e65bc6` [G6]\n- outbound auth/prior-art: `fd2b4ab546f9e330c` [T1] + `f252cc4922c662cc3` [T5c]\n- 3-way: `ff1e44af24964e2c6` [E4] + `f711f89314e759479` [G1G2] + `ff433167f9a0c74c5` [G6]\n- send-flow failure handling: `f71d6f4d69d9eda6e` [T5b] + `fa13c03bbc6396a28` [T6]\n\n**`ts-carbon-dsx-card-web-component`** (3 groups)\n- `fafd331051f282d48` [A1] + `fce6a492c25ad79d8` [G1G2]\n- 4-way: `fac2282ff04867c07` [E4] + `f73a2ac0bd5912fa0` [G1G2] + `fae54d7542a904816` [T1] + `f7cb2731aec88a265` [T3]\n- `f036b5d8ba8ce1922` [E4] + `f5677bcc33d08f796` [G1G2]\n\n**`jira-dso-legacy-code-remediation`** (2 groups, both 3-way)\n- `fefb33dc413d1ffce` [E2,T2] + `ff3ca4c59c47d2605` [T5a] + `f979dd7afcdc2675a` [G6]\n- `f183d47c0909708aa` [E2] + `fa60c9c99e3cf1eb4` [T5b] + `f979dd7afcdc2675a` [G6]\n\n**`scss-uswds-elements-dsx-token-migration`**: `fa397c3a9c775bb37` [E2] + `f2fe1f5b397e2040f` [G1G2]; `f8fbdb6fdf4b8abc3` [COH,E6] + `f164935f57c7fe71a` [G6]\n**`java-opensearch-adaptive-concurrency`**: `f5b48e0266cef5b37` [E2,E1] + `f45ee8af458d5e534` [A1]; `fec86f00ba47d9527` [G1G2] + `f6df8eee7ef8c8679` [T3]\n**`ruby-mn-deed-casemgmt-outbound-writeback`**: `fbda6e01e068e5510` [COH] + `f4439faeb93f9d19d` [E1]; `f8c8cc7182e9ee590` [E4] + `f72dae17551bf761a` [G1G2]\n**`jira-dso-strata-sdk-planning-context`**: `f596c92c78cf6b105` [G6] + `faf7819abb3a020d4` [T8]\n\nWorth noting for whoever picks this up: `f979dd7afcdc2675a` [G6] is **one** finding that was\nmerged into **two different** issues in the same run — it duplicates two distinct defects at once.\n\n## Fingerprints: they do NOT match\n\n**All 16 groups have fully distinct per-finding `id`s — 16/16 all-distinct, zero collisions.**\nSo whatever identity these ids carry, duplicate findings are not colliding on it and could not\nbe caught by equality on it.\n\nThere is no per-finding fingerprint field to compare. `material_fingerprint` exists only **once\nper run** at the top level of the verdict (e.g. `ca0fee4a8c160bf4`), not per finding.\n\n## Were duplicates dropped? No.\n\nThe verdict `dropped` list is populated — 7 entries on the `rfi` run — but **every drop is\n`reason: veto:cited-reference-inaccurate`**, a citation-accuracy veto. **No finding in any run\nwas dropped for duplication.** Every duplicate reached the emitted output.\n\n## Were they blocking? Yes — 22 of the ~35 member findings.\n\nThis is not confined to advisory noise. Whole groups are blocking on **every** copy:\n`scss-uswds` 1.1 and 3.1, `ts-carbon` 2.1 and 3.1, `rfi` 3.1 and 6.1, `mn-deed` 2.1,\n`dso-strata` 1.1, `java-opensearch` 5.1. Duplication therefore inflates the **blocking** count a\nplan author must answer, not just the advisory tail.\n\n## Other observations an investigator may want\n\n1. **Blocking eligibility diverges between copies of one issue.** `rfi` group 12.1:\n   `f02d0cd5760121153` has `blocking_enabled=false, block_threshold=0.95` while its duplicate\n   `f50f3f76a15e65bc6` has `blocking_enabled=true, block_threshold=0.6`. Same issue, different\n   eligibility and a threshold 0.35 apart. Also in `java-opensearch` 3.2, `dso-legacy` 10.1 and\n   14.1, `ts-carbon` 9.1, `mn-deed` 1.1.\n2. **Copies often carry identical confidence.** `rfi` 12.1: both `validity=0.75`, both\n   `priority=0.5025`. `ts-carbon` 2.1: all four at `validity=0.8`. `dso-legacy` 10.1: all three\n   at `0.875`. Not universal — `scss-uswds` 1.1 is 1.0 vs 0.9.\n3. **`cohort` is sometimes much wider than `criteria`.** `f02d0cd5760121153` has\n   `criteria=['T5b','T9']` but `cohort=['T2','T4','T5b','T5e','T7','T9']`.\n4. **Every criterion involved in a duplicate group is `blocking` or `advisory` per\n   `rebar explain`**; `G1G2`, `G6`, `E4`, `T1`, `T3`, `A1` are all `exec:AGENT`, while `E1`,\n   `E2`, `COH`, `T5b`, `T9` are `1-TURN`/`2-STEP`. Recorded as observation only.\n5. **Two runs show 0% inflation** (`java-gradle`, `java-iceberg`, plus `signal-coverage`), so\n   this is not unconditional.\n\n## Reproduction material\n\nVerdict JSONs: `~/plan-review-bakeoff/wave3/rebar-runs/<run-id>.verdict.json`.\nJudge-majority merges: `~/plan-review-bakeoff/artifacts/adjudications/<run-id>.adjudication.json`,\nfield `merged_issues` (members + arms), and `arms.rebar.same_arm_merges`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Root cause identified for why one defect is emitted as several findings under different criteria.\n- [ ] Stated explicitly whether any de-duplication step is expected to run before emission, and if so why it did not fire on these 16 groups.\n- [ ] Decision recorded on whether per-finding identity should support duplicate detection, given the observed ids are all distinct and `material_fingerprint` is per-run.\n- [ ] The divergent `blocking_enabled`/`block_threshold` between copies of one issue is explained or fixed.\n- [ ] Regression coverage over at least the `ts-carbon` (+50%) and `rfi` (+36%) cases.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nRoot-causing was deliberately **not** attempted here; this ticket is an evidence record.","id":"0110-bb37-caea-4d47","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Plan review emits one defect as several findings under different criteria (+14% finding inflation, up to +50%; duplicates not deduped and often blocking)"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789503166731996001,"uuid":"d82bc233-2699-446d-a52c-bbb597b48f04"}